Subject: [PATCH] Buffer advisory content-store writes instead of syncing each

Base: facebook/buck2 9a1876786f32806f6b65fc51f4c1c3077efc38a5 plus the
preceding Sekka patches.

Materializing a fresh worktree looks objects up one file at a time, and
each lookup recorded its LRU access and view hint in a FULL-synchronous
commit under the cross-process lock. A rebuild materializes ~22,500 files,
18,768 of them incremental state, so four worktrees queued on ~90,000
WAL syncs: 125-137 s each, against 37 s with the store off.

Accesses and hints are advisory, so they are now buffered in the
process and written, in order, with the next durable commit, before any
eviction decision (which therefore sees them), or after 256 entries or
one second. A cached lookup's transaction usually writes nothing and its
commit needs no sync. Object accounting is unchanged and stays FULL and
durable before canonical renames. A failed publication drops its
buffered hints. Buffered writes lost with a process only cost LRU order
and recovery hints.

